# KitarCash Code Review — Bugs & Issues Found

Full review of the codebase covering all components, services, pages, cloud functions, and Firestore rules.

---

## 🔴 Critical Bugs

### 1. [analyzeImage](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/services/geminiService.ts#12-89) silently returns `undefined` on failure
**File:** [geminiService.ts](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/services/geminiService.ts#L79-L88)

The function only returns inside the `if (jsonText)` block. If `jsonText` is falsy (empty/null), the function **implicitly returns `undefined`**, but the return type promises [EWasteItem](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/types.ts#7-19). This crashes downstream code in [Chatbot.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx) that tries to read `.itemName`, `.category`, etc.

```typescript
// Line 79–88: No return or throw in the else branch
if (jsonText) {
    const eWasteData: EWasteItem = JSON.parse(jsonText);
    return eWasteData; 
}
// ❌ Falls off the end — returns undefined, violating the Promise<EWasteItem> type
```

**Fix:** Add `throw new Error('No response from Gemini API')` after the `if` block.

---

### 2. [MapComponent](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#34-127) prop mismatch — `centers` prop passed but never received
**File:** [PickupScheduler.tsx:289](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#L289) ↔ [MapComponent.tsx:16-18](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#L16-L18)

[PickupScheduler](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#138-444) passes `<MapComponent centers={...} height="250px" />`, but [MapComponent](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#34-127) defines its props as `{ onDataLoaded?: ... }` — it **does not accept** `centers` or `height`. The `centers` prop is silently ignored, and the `height` is hardcoded to `300px` inside the component.

```tsx
// PickupScheduler.tsx line 289
<MapComponent centers={mockRecyclingCenters} height="250px" />

// MapComponent.tsx — actual interface
interface MapComponentProps {
  onDataLoaded?: (data: any[]) => void;  // ❌ No 'centers' or 'height'
}
```

**Impact:** The mock recycling center data is never used by the map; it fetches from Firestore instead. The map height cannot be overridden.

---

### 3. [handleCancelPickup](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#247-260) resets `currentRequestId` but not `poolStatus`
**File:** [PickupScheduler.tsx:247-259](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#L247-L259)

After cancelling, the code sets `setCurrentRequestId(null)` on line 252, but **never sets `setPoolStatus('cancelled')`**. It relies on the Firestore `onSnapshot` listener for that. However, since `currentRequestId` is now `null`, the listener **unsubscribes immediately** (line 160: `if (!currentRequestId) return;`). This creates a race:
- If the snapshot fires before the state updates → status changes to `cancelled` ✅
- If the state clears first → the listener is gone, and the UI **stays stuck** on `waiting`/`pooled` forever ❌

```typescript
// Line 252: clears the ID...
setCurrentRequestId(null);
// ...which kills the snapshot listener on line 160
// But poolStatus is never explicitly set to 'cancelled'
```

**Fix:** Add `setPoolStatus('cancelled')` inside [handleCancelPickup](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#247-260) before or after clearing the request ID.

---

### 4. `setUserRole` Cloud Function has NO authentication guard
**File:** [functions/src/index.ts:16-49](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/functions/src/index.ts#L16-L49)

The admin check is **commented out** (lines 19-21). Any authenticated user can call this function and give themselves the `admin`, `recycling_center`, or `driver` role. This is a **privilege escalation vulnerability**.

```typescript
// Lines 19-21: COMMENTED OUT
// if (request.auth?.token.role !== 'admin') {
//   throw new HttpsError('permission-denied', 'Only admins can set roles.');
// }
```

---

### 5. Firestore rules for `pickupRequests` are too permissive
**File:** [firestore.rules:49-51](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/firestore.rules#L49-L51)

```
match /pickupRequests/{requestId} {
  allow read, write: if request.auth != null;
}
```

Any authenticated user can **read, modify, or delete** any other user's pickup request. A malicious user could:
- Cancel other users' requests
- Change status to `completed` to trigger driver payouts
- Read all users' addresses and phone numbers

---

### 6. Firestore rules block driver reads of user data
**File:** [firestore.rules:7-8](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/firestore.rules#L7-L8)

```
match /users/{uid} {
  allow read: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == uid;
```

Only the user themselves can read their own doc. But [DriverDashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/pages/DriverDashboard.tsx) (line 28) does `getDoc(doc(db, "users", data.userId))` to fetch customer names/phones. This **will always be denied by Firestore rules** for drivers, causing the catch block to fire and showing "Customer" / "N/A" for every task.

---

## 🟡 Logic Bugs

### 7. [Chatbot.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx) references undeclared variable `isUploading` before it's defined
**File:** [Chatbot.tsx:117](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx#L117) vs [line 277](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx#L277)

[handleSendMessage](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/Chatbot.tsx#115-154) (line 117) checks `isUploading`, but `isUploading` is declared on line 277 (`const isUploading = uploadProgress !== null`). Due to hoisting behavior, `isUploading` won't work like a regular `const` inside the function body — this actually works at runtime because the `const` is evaluated before the callback runs, but it's fragile. However, there's a deeper issue:

`isUploading` is not reactive — it's computed once per render. If `uploadProgress` changes between when the user clicks send and when the handler executes, the check might be stale.

---

### 8. [handleSendManually](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#261-282) creates a transaction but `identifiedItem` check leads to wrong flow
**File:** [PickupScheduler.tsx:261-281](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#L261-L281)

If `identifiedItem` is `null`, the function just sets `option` to `'manual'` (line 263), which shows the recycling center list. But the button text says **"Send Manually"**, which implies the item should be submitted. The user sees recycling centers with no indication that their item wasn't processed.

Also, on error (line 279), it sets `option` to `'manual'` without any error message to the user — the transaction creation silently fails and shows the recycling center list.

---

### 9. Duplicate [getDistanceKm](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/services/firestoreService.ts#5-16) function
**Files:** [PickupScheduler.tsx:23](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#L23), [firestoreService.ts:5](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/services/firestoreService.ts#L5), [MapComponent.tsx:23](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/MapComponent.tsx#L23)

The Haversine formula is copy-pasted in **3 different files**. Not a bug per se, but a maintenance risk — if one is fixed, the others won't be.

---

### 10. Misleading comment for `setDefaultRole` function
**File:** [functions/src/index.ts:53-54](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/functions/src/index.ts#L53-L54)

The comment says `FUNCTION: verifyAndCredit` but the exported name is `setDefaultRole`. Copy-paste error:

```typescript
// ─── FUNCTION: verifyAndCredit ───  ← Wrong label
export const setDefaultRole = onCall(async (request) => {
```

---

### 11. `createTransaction` role check may block new users
**File:** [functions/src/index.ts:80-82](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/functions/src/index.ts#L80-L82)

```typescript
if (request.auth.token.role !== 'user') {
  throw new HttpsError('permission-denied', ...);
}
```

Custom claims are set in `setUserRole` or `setDefaultRole` Cloud Functions, but neither is called automatically during signup. [AuthContext](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/context/AuthContext.tsx#22-33) creates the Firestore doc with `role: 'user'`, but **never sets the custom claim on the Auth token**. So `request.auth.token.role` will be `undefined` for new users, causing `createTransaction` to **always fail** with "Only regular users can create transactions."

---

### 12. Google Sign-in button does nothing
**File:** [AuthCard.tsx:156-162](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#L156-L162)

The "Sign in with Google" button has no `onClick` handler — it's purely decorative. A user clicking it will see nothing happen.

---

### 13. Geolocation error not shown in [PickupScheduler](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#138-444) init
**File:** [PickupScheduler.tsx:149-156](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/PickupScheduler.tsx#L149-L156)

The initial `useEffect` to get the user's location has no error callback. If the user denies permission, `userLocation` stays `null` permanently, but the distances in the recycling center list silently fall back to the hardcoded `center.distance` with no indication the live distance failed.

---

### 14. Unused `navigate` import in [AuthCard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx)
**File:** [AuthCard.tsx:2,20](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/components/auth/AuthCard.tsx#L2)

`useNavigate` is imported and called (`const navigate = useNavigate()`) but `navigate` is never used anywhere in the component. Dead code.

