## 🟠 Data Safety Concerns

### 15. Firestore read rule for transactions may leak data to center staff
**File:** [firestore.rules:30-31](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/firestore.rules#L30-L31)

```
allow read: if request.auth != null
  && request.auth.token.role == 'recycling_center';
```

Any recycling center staff can read **all** transactions from **all** centers — not just their own. There's no check for `resource.data.centerId == request.auth.token.centerId`.

---

### 16. [.env](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/.env) file is checked into the repository
**File:** [.env](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/.env) (544 bytes)

The [.env](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/.env) file likely contains API keys (Firebase, Gemini, EmailJS). It's present in the project root and may be committed to Git if [.gitignore](file:///c:/Users/User/Desktop/KitarCash-demo/.gitignore) doesn't exclude it properly.

